redirector-hold-tcp

From: Victor Araújo <victor@victor-software-house.com>

Downstream-Reason: Divert only TCP to the extension, hold in-scope flows for a bounded time while no controller is attached instead of refusing them at once, and answer a status app message, so a router restart costs clients no retries and DNS never depends on the router.
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Drop-When: The redirector is replaced by the session-billing extension with declarative flow rules (OpenSpec follow-up to L1).
